docs/scratch/arrival-break/plan.md:5:Last session ratified the Sol architecture suite (`docs/architecture/arrival/`, five HTML docs) as the backend-neutral 1.0 full-break target: arrival is a **protocol** (one ordered, verifiable history per lineage, one authoritative append head), not a mandatory file — a `.arrival` file is one backend. Anchors: `decision:design/arrival-backend-neutral-protocol` (parent ruling + deletion list), `decision:design/arrival-wire-v1-seam-triage` (drop `body.t`, re-spell tick observer, keep dual signature), `decision:design/arrival-suite-review-dispositions` (witness minimum, counts optional, head-attestation naming, descriptor-in-`.vertex`, DuckDB-as-example). MERGE and ADOPT are ruled separable. This plan sequences the break end-to-end: merge the converged branch, execute the triage, extract the backend contract, build the witness minimum and migration sidecar, delete the legacy modes, adopt `.arrival` for live stores.
