docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-305-- **Counts omitted.** Dispositions §2: they are projection corroboration smuggled into a
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-306-  custody claim. Not optional-and-unset — absent from the type.
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-307-- **`sig`/`issuer`/`key_id`/`previous` absent.** Deferred grammar (dispositions §1). Their
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-308-  absence is the honest shape of an unsigned local cache; adding empty fields would advertise
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-309-  a claim this slice does not make.
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md:310:- **`protocol`/`wire` omitted from the record**, carried by the file header instead (B.3) —
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-311-  they are properties of the journal, not of each entry, and re-stating them per line is a
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-312-  field nothing reads. Same discipline the registry applied to `lineage`/`role`
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-313-  (`arrival_registry.py:94-97`): parsing fields nothing consumes is how speculative grammar
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-314-  ossifies.
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md:315:- **`observed_at` kept.** It is what makes a refusal actionable ("your cached head is from
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-316-  three weeks ago") and what answers audit staleness at open. §04 is explicit that it is
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-317-  witness metadata and never ledger order.
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-318-- **`level` is the scope-the-claim field** and it is the one addition to §04's table. It states
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-319-  how much was actually established, so an entry can never be read as a stronger claim than
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-320-  the evidence behind it. §12's checkpoint discussion asks for exactly this
docs/scratch/arrival-break/slice3-design-proposal.md-321-  (`witness-protocol.html:583-589`: a checkpoint retains "completion status").
